https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/labels/accepted","name":"accepted","color":"0052cc","default":false,"description":"There is consensus among the team that this change meets the criteria for inclusion"},{"id":829215248,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw4MjkyMTUyNDg=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/labels/archived%20due%20to%20age","name":"archived due to age","color":"eeeeee","default":false,"description":"This issue has been archived; please open a new issue for any further discussion"}],"state":"closed","locked":true,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":10,"created_at":"2015-06-19T03:40:19Z","updated_at":"2018-02-07T01:03:39Z","closed_at":"2015-06-24T17:01:12Z","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"###### Disclaimers:\n1. I've only just started my ES6 journey (so this could be my misinterpretation of `class` semantics)\n2. I'm using the [babel-eslint](https://github.com/babel/babel-eslint) parser, if that matters (although the same behaviour seems to occur with the default parser)\n###### Issue:\n\nGiven the class:\n\n```\n/*eslint semi: [2, \"always\"], no-extra-semi: 2*/\n\nclass Foo {\n  constructor() {\n    ...\n  }         // <- note: no semicolon after closing brace\n\n  bar() {\n    ...\n  };        // <- note: with semicolon after closing brace\n\n  baz() {\n    ...\n  }         // <- note: no semicolon after closing brace\n}\n```\n\n... no warnings are raised.  Should they be?\n\nIt would seem that semicolons are allowed, but optional, for ES6 class methods.\n\nIf so, I would have expected that either:\n1. the `semi` rule would complain about the missing semicolons on the `constructor()` and `baz()` methods; **or**\n2. the `no-extra-semi` rule would complain about the explicit semicolon after the `bar()` method?\n","closed_by":{"login":"nzakas","id":38546,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4NTQ2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38546?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas","html_url":"https://github.com/nzakas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/2794/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/2794/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}